          "name": "Rupturing Shriek",
          "kind": "action",
          "description": "Velicarn's head unleashes a horrific howl that causes blood to leak out of those who hear it and into his gaping open mouth. All creatures within 30 feet must succeed at a check (fortitude, dc:28, options:area-effect,inflicts:drained) save or become Drained 1 (Drained 2 on a critical failure) as some of their blood runs from their bodies into Velicarn's maw. Creatures currently taking persistent bleed damage take a –2 circumstance penalty to this saving throw. Velicarn's head regains 5 healing Hit Points for every creature in the area, to a maximum of 25 healing Hit Points, and he can't use Rupturing Shriek again for 1d4.",
