      "hardness": 0,
      "stealth": {
        "modifier": 25,
        "details": "(expert)"
      },
      "disable": "check (arcana, dc:25) (trained), check (nature, dc:25) (trained), or check (survival, dc:25) (trained) to divert the flow into weaker streams, or check (athletics, dc:27), check (crafting, dc:27) (trained), or check (thievery, dc:27) (trained) to break up the ground to weaken the flow; two successes (or one critical success) are needed to disable the hazard.",
      "isComplex": true,
      "routine": "(1 action) The hazard attempts an Athletics check with a +28 modifier to Shove all creatures in the water-filled areas in areas E5 and E6 toward the drop-off in area E7; the boiling spring gains a +4 circumstance bonus to its Fortitude DC against this effect. Any creature ending its turn in the flow also takes 2d12+12 fire damage with a check (fortitude, dc:29, basic) save.",
